  "headline": "Indonesian Police Prepare Appeal Process For Fired Generals",
  "seoTitle": "Indonesian Police Handle Appeals of Dismissed Generals",
  "metaDescription": "The Indonesian National Police are organizing ethics committees to hear appeals from two generals dismissed following illegal wiretapping allegations.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Police officials are establishing appellate ethics commissions for two dismissed generals.",
    "The officers were previously removed from service over alleged illegal wiretapping of President Prabowo Subianto.",
    "Both dismissed individuals filed formal appeals against their recent dishonorable discharge rulings."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian National Police (Polri) recently ordered the dishonorable discharge of two high-ranking officers, Inspector Generals Ahrie Sonta Nasution and Eko Hadi Santoso, following investigations into unauthorized surveillance. Ethics hearings concluded that the officers participated in a conspiracy to conduct illegal wiretapping activities targeting President Prabowo Subianto, utilizing police-issued equipment. Following their dismissal, both individuals submitted formal appeals against the decision, prompting the police headquarters to assemble special appellate committees to review the cases. Representatives from oversight bodies noted that the officers expressed regret and apologized during their initial disciplinary proceedings. While these officers await their appeal outcomes, the police have indicated that additional ethics proceedings related to other personnel and leadership figures are expected to continue in the coming weeks, reinforcing a departmental commitment to addressing professional misconduct without impunity.",
